WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.256
Continuous monitoring is the ongoing process of maintaining awareness of security posture, control effectiveness, system changes, vulnerabilities, threats, and risk.

2
00:00:11.256 --> 00:00:17.731
It is not the same as running one assessment before launch and then assuming the system remains safe.

3
00:00:17.731 --> 00:00:20.044
Modern systems change constantly.

4
00:00:20.044 --> 00:00:29.064
Assets appear, identities are added, configurations drift, vulnerabilities are disclosed, incidents occur, and business use evolves.

5
00:00:29.064 --> 00:00:32.919
Monitoring exists because security posture is not static.

6
00:00:32.919 --> 00:00:46.333
A useful continuous monitoring program watches the parts of the environment that influence risk: assets, identities, configurations, logs, vulnerabilities, incidents, changes, and control evidence.

7
00:00:46.333 --> 00:00:50.650
It connects technical signals to operational and risk decisions.

8
00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:54.890
That means monitoring should not stop at displaying dashboards.

9
00:00:54.890 --> 00:01:02.060
It should help people understand what changed, why it matters, who owns it, and what action should happen next.

10
00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:07.456
The word continuous does not mean every signal is reviewed every second by a person.

11
00:01:07.456 --> 00:01:13.701
It means monitoring is built into normal operations and repeated at a cadence that fits the risk.

12
00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:16.861
Some signals may need near-real-time alerting.

13
00:01:16.861 --> 00:01:21.641
Others may support periodic review, trend analysis, or audit readiness.

14
00:01:21.641 --> 00:01:29.428
The right rhythm depends on criticality, exposure, sensitivity, regulatory context, and how quickly risk can change.

15
00:01:29.428 --> 00:01:32.357
Continuous monitoring is decision support.

16
00:01:32.357 --> 00:01:35.210
A dashboard that no one uses is not a program.

17
00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:38.216
A scan result with no owner is not remediation.

18
00:01:38.216 --> 00:01:42.148
A log stream with no retention or review plan is not evidence.

19
00:01:42.148 --> 00:01:50.088
Effective monitoring connects data to triage, escalation, remediation, risk acceptance, reporting, and improvement.

20
00:01:50.088 --> 00:01:57.952
The purpose is not to collect the most data; it is to make better security and risk decisions faster and more consistently.
